# What keeps the old product name after the rename to Atlas (RENAME-ATLAS-1 and -2), read by
# scripts/rename_to_atlas.py and tests/test_atlas_rename.py. Everything else is renamed.
#   ## <group>: <reason>     starts a group; docs/plans/atlas-rename.md explains each one
#   file <glob>              the whole file keeps its bytes (its path is still renamed)
#   text <glob> <regex>      the spans the regex matches keep their text, in contents and paths
# Globs are fnmatch patterns on the renamed, repository-relative path (`*` crosses `/`).
# To rename a group later (its servers deleted, the website moved), delete its lines here and
# run scripts/rename_to_atlas.sh again.

## legacy-names: RENAME-ATLAS-2 renamed the cloud, server and Mac names; the old ones that the code still reads or cleans up for one release (DigitalOcean tags, droplet, snapshot, firewall and key names, the project, the account key and keychain entries, server paths and units, launchd labels, format ids) are written only here, and the operator's checklist lists them
file src/atlas/legacy_names.py
file tests/test_campaign_scope_legacy_names.py
file docs/operations/atlas-rename-checklist.md

## website: page paths, files and names of the Shifter website (its own repository); they change there first
text * (?<![\w.~$}/-])/proxy-index(?![\w-])
text * https?://(?:www\.)?shifter\.io/proxy-index(?![\w-])
text * (?:\b(?:src|scripts)/(?:[\w.\[\]-]+/)*|(?<![\w-])og/)proxy-index\b(?![-_])
text * \bProxyIndex\w+|\bproxyIndex\w+|\bproxy-index-home\.tsx\b
text * branch `proxy-index`

## external-repos: other repositories keep their names (the old, frozen API repository and the website's)
text * (?<!/)proxy-index-api\b
text * proxy-index-website\b

## checksummed: applied schema and migration files; their bytes (comments included) are recorded or applied in the databases
file src/atlas/schema.sql
file src/atlas/migrate_v*.sql
file src/atlas/calculated/migrate_v*.sql
file tests/fixtures/schema_v*.sql
file api/internal/store/migrations/*.sql

## history: dated reports record what ran at the time, with the names of the time
file docs/reports/*

## rename-tooling: the rename itself names what it renames
file scripts/rename_to_atlas.*
file tests/test_atlas_rename.py
text tests/test_ci_gates.py proxy[-_]index
text tests/test_server_setup.py "proxy[-_]index" not in
file docs/plans/atlas-rename.md
